="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133874803,imgsize-207013.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cox Enterprises protects 4,400 South Carolina acres worth hundreds of millions forever]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133883204.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cox-enterprises-gave-up-development-rights-on-nearly-4400-south-carolina-acres-worth-hundreds-of-millions-the-land-is-now-protected-forever-including-40-miles-of-river-and-marsh-frontage/articleshow/133883204.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cox-enterprises-gave-up-development-rights-on-nearly-4400-south-carolina-acres-worth-hundreds-of-millions-the-land-is-now-protected-forever-including-40-miles-of-river-and-marsh-frontage/articleshow/133883204.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T01:46:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133883372,imgsize-90109.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Antarctica gained 695 billion tons in 2021-23 as tropical warmth drove heavy snowfall]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133872390.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Between 2021 and 2023, Antarctica experienced a notable gain in ice mass, primarily driven by exceptional snowfall in East Antarctica. This unusual occurrence, influenced by warmer tropical ocean temperatures, caused atmospheric disturbances that transported moisture southward. Although this gain temporarily countered ongoing ice loss in other regions, it does not signify a change in Antarctica's long-term trend of declining ice mass.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/after-losing-about-140-5-billion-tons-of-ice-a-year-for-two-decades-antarctica-temporarily-reversed-course-gaining-a-record-695-billion-tons-in-2021-23-as-tropical-warmth-drove-heavy-snowfall/articleshow/133872390.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/after-losing-about-140-5-billion-tons-of-ice-a-year-for-two-decades-antarctica-temporarily-reversed-course-gaining-a-record-695-billion-tons-in-2021-23-as-tropical-warmth-drove-heavy-snowfall/articleshow/133872390.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133872719,imgsize-2025769.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[AI predicts fusion plasma instability 200 ms early, stops it in time]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133920366.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/princeton-put-ai-in-charge-of-a-fusion-plasma-control-loop-running-every-20-milliseconds-in-one-test-it-predicted-a-damaging-instability-200-ms-early-and-stopped-it-before-it-began/articleshow/133920366.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/princeton-put-ai-in-charge-of-a-fusion-plasma-control-loop-running-every-20-milliseconds-in-one-test-it-predicted-a-damaging-instability-200-ms-early-and-stopped-it-before-it-began/articleshow/133920366.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T00:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133920475,imgsize-46679.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Rachel Chen, 18, who won $100K for her breakthrough quantum math research using simple diagrams]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133936043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Rachel Chen, an 18-year-old Los Angeles student, won $100,000 at the Regeneron Science Talent Search for expanding a 1997 mathematical idea involving Temperley-Lieb diagrams. Her research offers a visual way to describe complex quantum particle systems and spin representations, potentially helping researchers better understand connections between different quantum-mechanical states.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-rachel-chen-the-18-year-old-los-angeles-student-who-expanded-a-1997-quantum-math-idea-to-describe-entire-particle-systems-with-simple-diagrams-she-won-100000/articleshow/133936043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-rachel-chen-the-18-year-old-los-angeles-student-who-expanded-a-1997-quantum-math-idea-to-describe-entire-particle-systems-with-simple-diagrams-she-won-100000/articleshow/133936043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T23:22:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133936286,imgsize-102403.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1973, Montana released a gall fly to control spotted knapweed; decades later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133935506.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Controlling invasive spotted knapweed biologically has initiated an unexpected ecological chain reaction. Gall flies, introduced as a control measure, have turned into a vital winter food source for deer mice, causing a surge in their populations and an uptick in hantavirus spread. Areas dense with knapweed report more infected mice than those with native grasslands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1973-montana-released-a-gall-fly-to-control-spotted-knapweed-decades-later-the-biocontrol-program-was-linked-to-over-3-times-more-hantavirus-positive-deer-mice/articleshow/133935506.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1973-montana-released-a-gall-fly-to-control-spotted-knapweed-decades-later-the-biocontrol-program-was-linked-to-over-3-times-more-hantavirus-positive-deer-mice/articleshow/133935506.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T23:07:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133935899,imgsize-1119681.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[She bought a Maine island to stop clear-cutting; 90 years after Audubon opened its first camp there]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133934130.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Hog Island Audubon Camp marks an impressive ninety years of promoting environmental education and research. Located in Maine, this island was rescued from deforestation by environmentalists Millicent Todd Bingham and Mabel Loomis Todd. The camp is also the birthplace of Project Puffin, which successfully revitalized seabird numbers. Today, it remains a vital training ground for future scientists, educators, and artists, with its influence extending to bird conservation throughout North America.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/she-bought-a-maine-island-to-stop-clear-cutting-90-years-after-audubon-opened-its-first-camp-there-the-330-acre-sanctuary-still-trains-conservationists/articleshow/133934130.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/she-bought-a-maine-island-to-stop-clear-cutting-90-years-after-audubon-opened-its-first-camp-there-the-330-acre-sanctuary-still-trains-conservationists/articleshow/133934130.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T22:56:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133935450,imgsize-792375.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Democrat urges House Speaker to sue Trump admin over triumphal arch, says Congress never approved funds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133935908.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-democrat-urges-house-speaker-to-sue-trump-admin-over-triumphal-arch-says-congress-never-approved-funds/articleshow/133935908.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-democrat-urges-house-speaker-to-sue-trump-admin-over-triumphal-arch-says-congress-never-approved-funds/articleshow/133935908.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T23:22:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133936433,imgsize-914933.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Andrew Flintoff lists his £6.75 million Cheshire mansion, bought from Phil Neville in 2021]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133932615.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[England cricket legend Andrew Flintoff has put his £6.75 million Cheshire mansion on the market, four years after his life-changing Top Gear car crash. Bought from former Manchester United star Phil Neville in 2021, the 10,000 sq ft luxury property features six bedrooms, six bathrooms, four floors, a pool, gym, cinema and games room.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/andrew-flintoff-puts-6-75-million-cheshire-mansion-on-market-bought-in-2021-from-phil-neville-4-years-after-top-gear-car-crash-10000-sq-ft-home-features-6-bedrooms-and-4-floors/articleshow/133932615.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/andrew-flintoff-puts-6-75-million-cheshire-mansion-on-market-bought-in-2021-from-phil-neville-4-years-after-top-gear-car-crash-10000-sq-ft-home-features-6-bedrooms-and-4-floors/articleshow/133932615.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T22:04:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133933068,imgsize-146386.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[5.3-magnitude quake hits Tibet as region reels from deadly flash floods]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133934172.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A magnitude 5.3 earthquake struck Tibet recently, following another tremor last week.  Devastating flash floods hit the Tibet-Nepal border on August 26, causing widespread destruction.  The disaster has raised concerns over the fragile Qinghai-Tibet Plateau environment.  Rising temperatures and glacier melt are cited as contributing factors to the floods.  Nepal's death toll from the floods has risen to 1,357 people.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/5-3-magnitude-quake-hits-tibet-as-region-reels-from-deadly-flash-floods/articleshow/133934172.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/5-3-magnitude-quake-hits-tibet-as-region-reels-from-deadly-flash-floods/articleshow/133934172.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T22:33:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133934576,imgsize-586293.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lindsay Clancy murder case: Lawyer asks Trump to pardon Massachusetts mother after mistrial]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133933636.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/lindsay-clancy-murder-case-lawyer-asks-trump-to-pardon-massachusetts-mother-after-mistrial/articleshow/133933636.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/lindsay-clancy-murder-case-lawyer-asks-trump-to-pardon-massachusetts-mother-after-mistrial/articleshow/133933636.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T22:17:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133933923,imgsize-623920.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Inside a $29M California mansion no one has ever lived in]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133931801.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A French-style manor in Rancho Santa Fe is now for sale at $29 million.  This newly built home features antique materials and custom artisan craftsmanship throughout.  The expansive residence includes a main house and a separate guest house on 3.66 acres.  It boasts a zero-edge pool, gardens, and breathtaking views from its terraces.  The manor comes fully furnished with art and antiques, ready for immediate occupancy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-california-woman-built-a-10363-sq-ft-french-style-mansion-with-centuries-old-materials-sourced-from-around-the-world-no-one-has-lived-in-it-and-it-is-now-asking-29m/articleshow/133931801.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-california-woman-built-a-10363-sq-ft-french-style-mansion-with-centuries-old-materials-sourced-from-around-the-world-no-one-has-lived-in-it-and-it-is-now-asking-29m/articleshow/133931801.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T21:28:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133932097,imgsize-335955.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists seeded clouds over China’s Muz Taw Glacier; fresh snow cut ice loss by 14% to 17%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133914955.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scientists tested cloud seeding over China’s Muz Taw Glacier in 2018 to create artificial snowfall and slow ice loss. The experiment used silver iodide generators to encourage snow formation. Researchers found that fresh snow made the glacier surface brighter and reduced the amount of ice lost over a short period. However, they said the results are preliminary and need further testing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/in-2018-scientists-seeded-clouds-over-chinas-muz-taw-glacier-to-make-snow-the-brighter-surface-was-followed-by-14-to-17-less-ice-loss-in-a-preliminary-experiment/articleshow/133914955.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/in-2018-scientists-seeded-clouds-over-chinas-muz-taw-glacier-to-make-snow-the-brighter-surface-was-followed-by-14-to-17-less-ice-loss-in-a-preliminary-experiment/articleshow/133914955.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T22:06:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133916194,imgsize-147163.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Anvith, Dubai student who watched his brother’s school commute and built a free carpool service]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133931767.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a bid to tackle traffic congestion, a student from Dubai has launched a unique carpooling website that connects commuters with similar routes through sophisticated algorithmic matching. Community Carpool now boasts over a thousand registered users in Dubai, ensuring user privacy by discreetly matching individuals until they agree to share rides. Notably, a local property developer has embraced this platform for its workforce, facilitating its growth.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/meet-anvith-yalamanchili-the-17-year-old-dubai-student-who-watched-his-brothers-school-commute-triple-to-45-minutes-and-built-a-free-carpool-service-that-drew-1000-sign-ups/articleshow/133931767.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/meet-anvith-yalamanchili-the-17-year-old-dubai-student-who-watched-his-brothers-school-commute-triple-to-45-minutes-and-built-a-free-carpool-service-that-drew-1000-sign-ups/articleshow/133931767.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T21:24:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133932055,imgsize-808609.cms"/></item></channel></rss>